  "Question": "\\(x_1\\) and \\(x_2\\) are the two roots of \\(x²-3x-5=0\\). Find the value of \\(x_1²+x_2²\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "19",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(x_1+x_2=3\\), \\(x_1x_2=-5\\), and \\(x_1²+x_2²=(x_1+x_2)²-2x_1x_2=9+10=19\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Replace each square using the equation\n\nEach root satisfies the original equation, so its square can be replaced by a linear expression:\n\\[\nx_1^2=3x_1+5,\\qquad x_2^2=3x_2+5.\n\\]\nAdding these equations reduces the desired value to the root sum. The root-coefficient relation gives \\(x_1+x_2=3\\), hence\n\\[\nx_1^2+x_2^2=3(x_1+x_2)+10=3\\cdot3+10=19.\n\\]",
